,title,link,text,language,family
0,Bhadarwahi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhadarwahi_language,"Bhadarwahi (Bhadrawahi) is an indigenous language of the Indian subcontinent, belonging to the Western Pahari group. It is spoken by the Bhadarwahi people in the Bhadarwah region of Jammu and Kashmir, India.",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
1,"Bhadarwahi - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia",https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhadarwahi,"Bhadarwahi is a dialect of Punjabi, spoken in the Bhadarwah region of Jammu and Kashmir, India. It is an Indo-Aryan language from the Western Pahari languages. There are also some speakers in Pakistan.",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
2,Bhadrawahi | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bhd/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..5SBJnaIWVsq-ZeC_6Kt8rUU7jM1dLXp7X4qTmnId0tc,"Bhadrawahi is a stable indigenous language of India. It belongs to the Indo-European language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
3,Bhadrawahi (Davar Partners International) | South Asia Bibles,https://www.southasiabibles.com/resource/language/bhadrawahi,"Bhadrawahi is an Indo-Aryan language of the Western Pahari group spoken in the Bhadarwah region of Jammu and Kashmir, India. The name Bhadarwahi can be understood either in a narrow sense as referring to the dialect, locally known as Bhiḍlāi, native to the Bhadarwah valley...",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
4,Category:Bhadrawahi terms derived from Indo-European languages...,https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Bhadrawahi_terms_derived_from_Indo-European_languages,"Bhadrawahi terms that originate from one of the Indo-European languages. This category should, ideally, contain only other categories. Entries can be categorized here, too, when the proper subcategory is unclear.",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
5,The ASJP Database - Wordlist Bhadrawahi,https://asjp.clld.org/languages/BHADRAWAHI,Wordlist Bhadrawahi. JSON. RDF serialized as n3.,Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
6,Jambu | Language Bhadrawahi,https://neojambu.herokuapp.com/languages/bhad,Bhadrawahi [bhad]. Family. W. Pahari.Source Language Dravidian Indo-Aryan Munda Nuristani — Arabic English Persian Turkic.,Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
7,Bhadrawahi in India | UNESCO WAL,https://en.wal.unesco.org/en/countries/india/languages/bhadrawahi,"Video, film. Sound/music recording. Publishing activities.",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
8,Glottolog 5.3 - Bhadrawahi,https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/bhad1241,"collapse all. Indo-European (586). Bhadrawahi (1598-bhd) = Vulnerable (20 percent certain, based on the evidence available) [van Driem 2007](cldf:driem:07).",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
9,Bhadrawahi,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Bhadrawahi.htm,"Other comments: Bhadrawahi has a decimal system similar to that of some Western Pahari languages, the language is mainly spoken approximately 110,000 speakers in Jammu, with only a few speakers in Himachal Pradesh, and the autonym is भड्लाई Bʰaḍḷāī.",Bhadrawahi,Indo-European
